{
  "schema_version": "report-evidence/1",
  "source_sha256": "939d2a262ac90da379ae175d57630abc6326e96d1a7c901a27ccbb2eebefe05a",
  "fragments": [
    {
      "id": "e_939d2a262ac9_0001",
      "text": "Unprotected `init()` allows builder admin takeover and token drain",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 66,
      "line": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e_939d2a262ac9_0002",
      "text": "## Finding description and impact",
      "start": 68,
      "end": 101,
      "line": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "e_939d2a262ac9_0003",
      "text": "The `BuilderWallet.init()` function is an **unprotected external function** with no access control that can be called by anyone, multiple times. This enables an attacker to hijack the `builderAdmin` role and gain complete control of the wallet, including the ability to call `sweep()` and steal all accumulated tokens.",
      "start": 102,
      "end": 420,
      "line": 4
    },
    {
      "id": "e_939d2a262ac9_0004",
      "text": "1. `init()` is external with no access control or reentrancy protection",
      "start": 423,
      "end": 494,
      "line": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "e_939d2a262ac9_0005",
      "text": "2. Can be called by **anyone** and **multiple times**",
      "start": 495,
      "end": 548,
      "line": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "e_939d2a262ac9_0006",
      "text": "3. `builderAdmin` controls who can call `sweep()` and steal tokens",
      "start": 549,
      "end": 615,
      "line": 9
    },
    {
      "id": "e_939d2a262ac9_0007",
      "text": "### Attack Flow",
      "start": 617,
      "end": 632,
      "line": 11
    },
    {
      "id": "e_939d2a262ac9_0008",
      "text": "**Step 1: Owner initiates deployment**",
      "start": 634,
      "end": 672,
      "line": 13
    },
    {
      "id": "e_939d2a262ac9_0009",
      "text": "**Step 2: Owner's call gets mempool visibility**",
      "start": 674,
      "end": 722,
      "line": 15
    },
    {
      "id": "e_939d2a262ac9_0010",
      "text": "Attacker sees the pending transaction and can:",
      "start": 723,
      "end": 769,
      "line": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "e_939d2a262ac9_0011",
      "text": "1. Calculate the BuilderWallet address using public `predictBuilderWallet(12345)`",
      "start": 770,
      "end": 851,
      "line": 17
    },
    {
      "id": "e_939d2a262ac9_0012",
      "text": "2. Front-run or race the owner's `init()` call",
      "start": 852,
      "end": 898,
      "line": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "e_939d2a262ac9_0013",
      "text": "**Step 3: Attack execution**",
      "start": 900,
      "end": 928,
      "line": 20
    },
    {
      "id": "e_939d2a262ac9_0014",
      "text": "### Impact",
      "start": 930,
      "end": 940,
      "line": 22
    },
    {
      "id": "e_939d2a262ac9_0015",
      "text": "- All tokens accumulated in BuilderWallet can be stolen",
      "start": 941,
      "end": 996,
      "line": 23
    },
    {
      "id": "e_939d2a262ac9_0016",
      "text": "- Builder fee shares lost",
      "start": 997,
      "end": 1022,
      "line": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "e_939d2a262ac9_0017",
      "text": "- Protocol loses builder incentive revenue",
      "start": 1023,
      "end": 1065,
      "line": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "e_939d2a262ac9_0018",
      "text": "## Recommended mitigation steps",
      "start": 1067,
      "end": 1098,
      "line": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "e_939d2a262ac9_0019",
      "text": "Move init to constructor.",
      "start": 1100,
      "end": 1125,
      "line": 29
    }
  ]
}
